    "lore": "The Hellenic State was born in the fires of World War Two, and even in this new age, it still suffers from the same problems it had when Europe was engulfed by conflict. A deeply unpopular and undemocratic government, the recent history of Greece is characterized by a consistent failure to reform or liberalize the country in any way, as the state is kept together only by the heavy presence of Triumvirate garrisons to keep the numerous partisan groups and organizations in check. However, with the Prime Minister's health ailing, a crisis seems to be inevitable - and the cradle of European civilization might soon be engulfed by war once more. Will Greece manage to resurrect from her ashes as a phoenix, or is the country doomed to more decades of darkness?"
  },
